    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0456" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/92.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister to
                        Haiti</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In regard to your December 2,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d485-f1"/> January 8, and No.
                    993 of December 23<anchor n="2" xml:id="d485-f2"/>, the Department is gratified
                    to know that the Haitian Government has taken vigorous measures against the
                    Dominican revolutionists, <pb facs="0457" n="341" xml:id="pg341"/> and that it
                    is willing to broaden the powers of the boundary plenipotentiary. Similar action
                    is being urged at Santo Domingo by our Legation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
